{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793473481,"nonce":"GCTw0pK2R58fg+rNjTY/JdIAEIE=","title":"Embedding: a host cannot stop a running script","message":"Reported by the dynASB embedding session (their git-bug 5b7d11d). TieredRuntime::call_raw and the Lua state have no instruction budget, deadline or interrupt flag, so `while true do end` in a handler holds its thread until the process is killed. A host running untrusted scripts needs a per-call budget or a flag compiled loops poll; zylua's own SIGINT handling (f50d4b6) needs the same poll in loops.","files":null}]}